# ArduCopter 4.7.2 (Pixhawk 6C Mini): cuVSLAM VIO from the Jetson as EKF3 SOURCE SET 2 (indoors), set 1 untouched
# (GPS + compass, outdoors). Names checked against the Copter-4.7.2 source (2026-10-27). NOT applied automatically:
#   scripts/ardupilot_params.py vio_bringup/config/ardupilot_vio_params.parm            (dry run: current vs new)
#   scripts/ardupilot_params.py vio_bringup/config/ardupilot_vio_params.parm --write    (props off, then reboot)
#
# This drone's serial ports (read 2026-10-27): SERIAL0 USB MAVLink, SERIAL1 TELEM1 ESC telemetry, SERIAL2 TELEM2 RC
# receiver (CRSF/ELRS 420k), SERIAL3 GPS, SERIAL4 telemetry radio (MAVLink 57600), SERIAL7 2nd USB MAVLink. No UART is
# free: the Jetson connects by USB (SERIAL0, already MAVLink -> /dev/ttyACM0 on the Jetson). Do NOT turn SERIAL2 into
# MAVLink: that is the RC link.
#
# The feed: cuvslam.launch.py autopilot:=ardupilot -> vio_to_px4 -> /mavros/odometry/out -> MAVROS -> MAVLink ODOMETRY
# (frame LOCAL_FRD / child BODY_FRD - ArduPilot drops any other frame) over USB.
# Indoors, switch the EKF to source set 2 before arming: an RC switch (RCn_OPTION 90 = EKF Pos Source: low/mid/high
# = set 1/2/3) or MAV_CMD_SET_EKF_SOURCE_SET (42007) param1 = 2.

# --- Telemetry streams on the USB port (MAV1 = SERIAL0) for MAVROS on the Jetson: IMU for the obstacle scan, local
#     position / velocity for odom_tf and the VIO consistency check. (Mission Planner on USB gets them too.)
MAV1_RAW_SENS 20
MAV1_EXT_STAT 2
MAV1_POSITION 20
MAV1_EXTRA1 30
MAV1_EXTRA2 4
MAV1_EXTRA3 2

# --- Visual odometry over MAVLink
VISO_TYPE 1
# pose is reported for imu_link = the flight controller itself: no lever arm
VISO_POS_X 0
VISO_POS_Y 0
VISO_POS_Z 0
# camera capture -> ODOMETRY at the FC (cuVSLAM + MAVROS + USB), roughly
VISO_DELAY_MS 50
# 0 = take good or unknown quality (MAVROS sends 0); the bridge itself withholds bad frames
VISO_QUAL_MIN 0

# --- EKF3 source set 2 = indoors on VIO (ArduPilot's recommended ExternalNav setup: height from the barometer)
EK3_SRC2_POSXY 6
EK3_SRC2_VELXY 6
EK3_SRC2_POSZ 1
EK3_SRC2_VELZ 6
EK3_SRC2_YAW 6

# --- Payload winch (mission_supervisor drop_mechanism winch): N20 gear motor on a Cytron MDD20A, channel 1.
#     FMU PWM 5 (GPIO 54 = SERVO13) -> MDD20A PWM1: high = run, low = brake.  RELAY1 (MAVLink relay instance 0)
#     FMU PWM 6 (GPIO 55 = SERVO14) -> MDD20A DIR1: the direction.             RELAY2 (instance 1)
#     + a common GND between the Pixhawk FMU rail and the MDD20A. 3.3 V logic is enough for the MDD20A inputs.
#     The FMU outputs follow the IO outputs (MAIN 1-8 = SERVO1-8) as SERVO9..14: check that SERVO13 / SERVO14 are
#     not motors on this frame before writing. Feed the MDD20A at the N20's rated voltage (6 / 12 V BEC), not the
#     raw battery: the relays drive it at 100 % duty. Relays are not blocked by the safety switch or disarm: props off
#     for the bench test (ros2 service call /mission/winch std_srvs/srv/SetBool "{data: true}").
SERVO13_FUNCTION -1
SERVO14_FUNCTION -1
RELAY1_FUNCTION 1
RELAY1_PIN 54
RELAY1_DEFAULT 0
RELAY2_FUNCTION 1
RELAY2_PIN 55
RELAY2_DEFAULT 0
